[[:db/retract 17592186087969 :question/answer-fields 17592186084548] [:db/retract 17592186055075 :question/answer-fields 17592186051933] {:db/id 17592186087969 :question/worked-solution "To determine which of the following differential equations is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation, we attempt to write each option in the standard form.\n\nA first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nLet's attempt to write $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-{x}^{2}=\\frac{1}{1-y}$ in the standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-{x}^{2}=\\frac{1}{1-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{y-1}={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation cannot be written in standard form since the power of $y$ in the term $\\frac{1}{y-1}$ is not $1.$ Since the equation cannot be written in standard form, we conclude that it is not a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations can be written in the standard form, and therefore they are first-order linear ODEs." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-05fa89b3-8d8c-5d7d-a143-81330cce5025"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-05fa89b3-8d8c-5d7d-a143-81330cce5025" :answer-field/id #uuid "05fa89b3-8d8c-5d7d-a143-81330cce5025" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4da0e1b1-496c-56ae-a84c-c4de8d1b4756" :answer-field/choices ["answer-346b10b5-2bec-56ce-ae2c-3edb9c4195a9" "answer-0ba1699a-1266-5d2a-83a1-9ef98174bfab" "answer-c5d36e89-9f24-5514-94a7-4cfb223701bb" "answer-4da0e1b1-496c-56ae-a84c-c4de8d1b4756" "answer-1d712324-050d-5573-a4a5-5a0cca8602dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-346b10b5-2bec-56ce-ae2c-3edb9c4195a9" :answer/id #uuid "346b10b5-2bec-56ce-ae2c-3edb9c4195a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4xy=\\sqrt{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ba1699a-1266-5d2a-83a1-9ef98174bfab" :answer/id #uuid "0ba1699a-1266-5d2a-83a1-9ef98174bfab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5d36e89-9f24-5514-94a7-4cfb223701bb" :answer/id #uuid "c5d36e89-9f24-5514-94a7-4cfb223701bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{{e}^{x}}{x}y={x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4da0e1b1-496c-56ae-a84c-c4de8d1b4756" :answer/id #uuid "4da0e1b1-496c-56ae-a84c-c4de8d1b4756" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-{x}^{2}=\\frac{1}{1-y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d712324-050d-5573-a4a5-5a0cca8602dc" :answer/id #uuid "1d712324-050d-5573-a4a5-5a0cca8602dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-{x}^{2}y=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055075 :question/problem "If $A={1,4,7,…,295},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n1,\\,4,\\,7,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =3 \\\\  & =4-1 \\\\  & =7-4 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =1+(n-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =1+3n-3 \\\\  & =3n-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={3n-2:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3N-2 & =295 \\\\ 3N & =297 \\\\ N & =\\frac{297}{3} \\\\ N & =99\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={3n-2:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 99}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $99$ elements, we must have $|A|=99.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6d1ecda9-5e5d-5279-94e3-8d19798d2cd7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6d1ecda9-5e5d-5279-94e3-8d19798d2cd7" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d1ecda9-5e5d-5279-94e3-8d19798d2cd7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2689b7d1-3603-5132-aeff-4013c7212585" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2689b7d1-3603-5132-aeff-4013c7212585"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2689b7d1-3603-5132-aeff-4013c7212585" :answer/id #uuid "2689b7d1-3603-5132-aeff-4013c7212585" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "99" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-248e0d07-4285-57ca-807a-b5e68115c826" :activity/id #uuid "248e0d07-4285-57ca-807a-b5e68115c826" :activity/title "Quiz 1" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-697e509b-0d1c-5004-bdfe-d3a6ceea2429" "step-1b97548a-a5f3-5688-91a0-04cbb9b9eede" "step-414984ea-b6c3-522e-9f02-f339f1d5350e" "step-13167817-bd65-5732-a491-0bac1d6e32a7" "step-3880c31f-b525-52e8-8049-23194339b18e" "step-30656c66-70e9-5de6-a248-74d016e8cad6"] :activity/first-step "step-697e509b-0d1c-5004-bdfe-d3a6ceea2429" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-697e509b-0d1c-5004-bdfe-d3a6ceea2429" :step/id #uuid "697e509b-0d1c-5004-bdfe-d3a6ceea2429" :step/content 17592186087969 :step/next "step-1b97548a-a5f3-5688-91a0-04cbb9b9eede" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1b97548a-a5f3-5688-91a0-04cbb9b9eede" :step/id #uuid "1b97548a-a5f3-5688-91a0-04cbb9b9eede" :step/content 17592186409515 :step/next "step-414984ea-b6c3-522e-9f02-f339f1d5350e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-414984ea-b6c3-522e-9f02-f339f1d5350e" :step/id #uuid "414984ea-b6c3-522e-9f02-f339f1d5350e" :step/content 175921